spec={'openapi':'3.0.3','info':{'title':'Amentorz Sprint 1 API — review draft','version':'0.1.0-draft','description':'''PROPOSED CONTRACT ONLY. No client acceptance approval evidence supplied. No endpoint implementation implied. x-review-status separates ready-for-review from decision-required operations. Backend docs/openapi.yaml is the sole proposed Amentorz contract; existing JSDoc Swagger describes legacy template behavior and is not this draft. All paths below are relative to /api/v1. No booking, payment, live-session, earnings, scoring, messaging or infrastructure-control endpoints.

Existing envelope retained: success/message/data/meta; errors use success=false/message/errors/traceId (no new error-code field). Unknown fields rejected; strict Zod DTO validation proposed for every body, query and path. Strings trimmed before length checks except credentials; identifiers UUID, UTC RFC3339 timestamps. 422 validation, 409 conflict, 401 authentication, 403 permission/CSRF, 404 concealed resources. All protected responses and auth challenges use Cache-Control: no-store. Credentials never logged. Every unsafe request requires signed _csrf cookie plus x-csrf-token, even when unauthenticated. CSRF is additional to authentication, never a replacement.

Proposed authentication reuses HttpOnly JWT access/refresh cookies, same-origin frontend rewrite, SameSite=Strict, Secure in deployed HTTPS, no Domain. No JSON token delivery/localStorage. Access cookie Path=/; refresh Path=/api/v1/auth. PostgreSQL session family and token hashes are authoritative; every protected request checks live user activity, role and session version. Immediate server revocation on logout, password reset/change, account deactivation and any existing role change; refresh rotation and replay revoke family. Fail closed when authoritative checks unavailable. Proposed 15-minute access / seven-day absolute session / five-minute recent reauthentication, six-digit email OTP / 10-minute expiry / five attempts / 60-second resend cooldown / five sends per hour require approval. Refresh/logout/session-management routes remain usable during faculty onboarding restrictions. No public faculty/admin registration or role elevation API. Initial admin is an operator-only, audited provisioning command with prompted or secure-secret input, never a public endpoint or seeded password.

Public faculty eligibility is active user AND verified email AND active faculty profile AND current required terms accepted AND approved AND published AND at least one active valid assignment. This is a shared prerequisite for future bookability, not a guarantee of future booking, payment or attendance eligibility. Future bookability also rechecks selected assignment/price and later-sprint rules. All moderation and eligibility checks apply to content bytes as well as listings. Configuration/catalogue/pricing changes audit actor, UTC time and redacted values. Infrastructure backups, CI and deployment are operational procedures, not new API endpoints.'''} ,'servers':[{'url':'/api/v1','description':'Same-origin API; local frontend rewrite to backend. Deployment gateway must preserve auth cookie path.'}],'tags':[{'name':t,'description':d} for t,d in [(AUTH,'Task 1: identity, sessions and recovery.'),(CONSENT,'Student onboarding: legal policies and parent/guardian consent signing.'),(FAC,'Task 2: faculty onboarding and minimal publication reads.'),(CAT,'Task 3: configurable catalogue and faculty assignments.'),(PRICE,'Task 3: INR single 60-minute session pricing only.'),(LIB,'Task 3: decision-gated moderation and protected content.'),(CONF,'Task 4: typed non-secret business settings.'),('Audit','Tasks 1 and 4: restricted read-only audit access.')]],'security':[{'cookieAuth':[]}],'paths':P,'components':{'securitySchemes':{'cookieAuth':{'type':'apiKey','in':'cookie','name':'accessToken','description':'HttpOnly JWT access cookie; live server session/role checks required. No browser-readable bearer token workflow proposed.'},'refreshCookie':{'type':'apiKey','in':'cookie','name':'refreshToken','description':'HttpOnly rotating refresh cookie, Path=/api/v1/auth. Only for refresh; CSRF still mandatory.'}},'parameters':{'CsrfHeader':{'name':'x-csrf-token','in':'header','required':True,'description':'Token from GET /auth/csrf-token; must match signed HttpOnly _csrf cookie. Required for all unsafe methods including public auth.','schema':string(100)}},'responses':errors,'schemas':S}}
def sample(schema, field='', depth=0):
    if '$ref' in schema: return sample(S[schema['$ref'].rsplit('/',1)[1]],field,depth+1)
    if 'example' in schema: return schema['example']
    if 'enum' in schema: return schema['enum'][0]
    if 'oneOf' in schema: return sample(schema['oneOf'][0],field,depth+1)
    if schema.get('type')=='object':
        return {k:sample(v,k,depth+1) for k,v in schema.get('properties',{}).items() if k in schema.get('required',[]) and not v.get('writeOnly')}
    if schema.get('type')=='array': return []
    if schema.get('type')=='boolean': return field != 'isPublished'
    if schema.get('type') in ['integer','number']: return schema.get('minimum',1)
    if schema.get('format')=='date': return '2024-06-01'
    if schema.get('format')=='uri': return 'https://example.org/learning/algebra'
    return {'name':'Mathematics','fullName':'Ananya Rao','studentFullName':'Ananya Rao','title':'Algebra practice','institution':'Example University','organization':'Example College','position':'Lecturer','bio':'Mathematics tutor with experience teaching secondary school students.','code':'mathematics','key':'security.otpTtlSeconds','version':'faculty-terms-v1-review-only','content':'Approved terms text is required before implementation.','syllabus':'Linear equations and introductory algebra.','description':'Reviewed configuration definition.','reason':'Profile documents reviewed.','message':'Success','traceId':'review-example-trace','userAgent':'Example browser'}.get(field,'Example value')
for path,item in P.items():
    for method,operation in item.items():
        for code,response in operation['responses'].items():
            media=response.get('content',{}).get('application/json')
            if code.startswith('2') and media and 'example' not in media:
                value=sample(media['schema'])
                # Do not publish example secret/credential/token values, even synthetic ones.
                if not any(k in json.dumps(value) for k in ['resetCredential','csrfToken','consentToken','emailVerificationToken']):
                    if 'login' in operation['operationId']:
                        portal=operation['operationId'][5:].lower()
                        value['data']['user']['roles']=[{'id':uuid['example'],'name':portal,'permissions':[]}]
                    def fix_faculty(v):
                        if isinstance(v,dict):
                            if 'approvalStatus' in v and 'eligibility' in v:
                                v['acceptedTermsVersion']=None
                                v['acceptedTermsAt']=None
                                v['eligibility']={'visible':False,'eligibleForFutureBooking':False,'reasons':['TERMS_REQUIRED','NOT_APPROVED','NOT_PUBLISHED','NO_ACTIVE_ASSIGNMENT']}
                            for child in v.values(): fix_faculty(child)
                        elif isinstance(v,list):
                            for child in v: fix_faculty(child)
                    fix_faculty(value)
                    media['example']=value
(ROOT/'openapi.yaml').write_text(json.dumps(spec,indent=2)+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
lines=['# Sprint 1 endpoint index','', 'Review draft only. All paths are relative to `/api/v1`. `ready-for-review` is a review status, not evidence of approval or implementation. See [design](sprint-1-contract-review.md) for cross-cutting rules and open decisions.','']
for tag in spec['tags']:
    lines += ['## '+tag['name'],'','| Method | Path | Operation ID | Access | Review status |','|---|---|---|---|---|']
    for path,item in P.items():
        for method,operation in item.items():
            if tag['name'] in operation['tags']:
                lines.append('| '+ ' | '.join([method.upper(),'`'+path+'`','`'+operation['operationId']+'`',operation['x-required-role'],operation['x-review-status']])+' |')
    lines.append('')
(ROOT/'sprint-1-endpoints.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines),encoding='utf-8')
print(f'Wrote {len(P)} paths, {sum(len(v) for v in P.values())} operations, {len(S)} schemas. JSON serialization is valid YAML 1.2 and avoids a new authoring dependency.')
